  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-26 by an independent auditor who authored none of the change, after 394bd1e802 and 180b306ffa (spec-bgp-rs-replacement-on-withdrawal). RFC 8277 Section 2.4: \"Upon reception, the value of the Compatibility field MUST be ignored.\" rs server_handlers.go sendBatchedWithdrawals now carries the departed session generation in withdrawalGroup and passes it to recoverRouteSel, and rs handleStateDown stamps it on each entry and hands the map to a coalescing departure worker (merge: later entry wins per withdrawalKey). Neither touches how a VPN or labeled withdrawal key or its retained native hex is formed: withdrawalKey and entry.wire are built exactly as before, so a withdrawal still matches its announcement whatever Compatibility value it carried. rr handleStateDown gained the generation argument; the rr unit TestVPNReflectorPeerDownEmitsOnlyRetainedNativeRoutes changed only to pass 7, with every input (0x800000-Compatibility withdrawal, both families, with and without ADD-PATH) and every exact-hex assertion unchanged (independent judge approval recorded in 394bd1e802). The revert records on rr handleStateDown and rs sendBatchedWithdrawals were re-taken in 394bd1e802 with reds observed and verify under ./le rfc check. All other tagged units and cited producers (text_json.go, familyrib.go, mpwire.go) are byte-identical; rs and rr TestVPN*/TestLabeled* green at HEAD in an export. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history.",
